'''Dungeons''' are Player versus Environment (PvE) game modes, similar to [[Raids]], to acess the dungeons, the player should talk to [[Lucien]] or acess in the server page. To begin a dungeon, two or more players (four maximum) must gather in one of the three turnstiles in the [[Simulation Hub]]. Once started, the players are teleported to a separate game instance where they must progress through 15 consecutive rooms filled with [[enemies]]. Hard difficulty consists of 20 rooms, while Challenge difficulty consists of 100 rooms.

On Challenge difficulty, the player is restricted by a time limit of 15 minutes. Every floor cleared adds 30 seconds to the timer. There are no bosses after [[Zero]]; instead, the floors contain powerful [[enemies]] capable of defeating the player with a single attack.

==Mechanics==
The [[enemies]] encountered throughout the dungeon may come from various islands across the [[First Sea]], [[Second Sea]], and [[Third Sea]], along with new enemies exclusive to dungeons. These enemies are able to use dashes to move away if the player is attacking. Special boss rooms appear at specific intervals:
* '''Room 5''': [[Ancient Beast]]
* '''Room 10''': [[Kitsune Lord]]
* '''Room 15''': [[Gas Knight]]
* '''Room 20''': [[Zero]]

