After completing each room, the player is presented with three buff options and may choose one to apply. These buffs stack across all rooms, allowing the player to accumulate up to 15 (or 20-100 on higher difficulties) buffs by the final room. Buffs can increase specific stats by 500 points, enhance damage of particular weapons, reduce cooldowns, increase [[Air Jump|air jumps]], or grant special abilities such as life leech.

==Rewards==
At the end of the final room, or at the end of the timer on Challenge difficulty, the player is rewarded with a random [[Trinkets|trinket]] and a sum of {{Money|Money}}, [[Simulation Data]], random [[Materials]], and {{Fragment|Fragment}}s, depending on the damage dealt. After the rewards are distributed, the player is automatically teleported back to the [[Simulation Hub]]. Completing Hard or Challenge difficulty can reward up to three [[trinkets]].

Several nuances affect trinket rewards:

* Only a complete clear grants a chance at a [[Trinkets|trinket]]. Defeating [[bosses]] without finishing the dungeon does not reward any trinkets, and leaving before completion removes any chance of a reward. The player must finish the entire run for it to count.
* [[Trinkets]] can only be obtained from dungeons (unless the player buys [[Simulation Data]] from the [[Shop]] and uses it to roll trinkets from the [[Trinket Expert]]), which makes them mandatory content for players seeking a complete trinket set.
* Higher difficulty increases the odds of receiving more [[trinkets]], but there is no guaranteed drop system. Consistent, frequent runs generally provide more progress than infrequent attempts at a difficulty above the player's ability. However, Hard and Challenge Dungeons are the only way to obtain trinkets with modifiers without manually collecting enough of the same trinket to upgrade to Grade III.
* Even at the same reward tier on Challenge difficulty, the number of [[trinkets]] received (one, two, or three) is not fixed (except for the Bronze tier, which always rewards one trinket). Twenty separately documented Platinum-tier Challenge runs that both reached floor 100 yielded a different [[Trinkets|trinket]] count (two and three respectively), confirming that reaching a high floor count or a high reward tier does not guarantee the maximum number of trinkets.
* The reward scales with the team's total damage dealt rather than simply with completing the dungeon. A run in which a player deals little damage while relying on teammates yields a smaller reward than a run in which the player contributes damage throughout every room. Assigning roles in advance — such as who tanks, who deals the primary damage, and who handles stuns — can improve outcomes.

==Damage and Stats==
It is important to note that player damage inside a dungeon does not rely on their normal in-game [[Stats|stats]]. By default, all players deal damage as if they have 2,800 points in [[Melee]], [[Swords|Sword]], [[Guns|Gun]], and [[Blox Fruits|Blox Fruit]]. This base damage can be modified through the buffs obtained during the run. In addition, the player receives 350 additional defense stats (1,750 health) and extra [[Energy]] per room cleared. The player's damage also increases by a set amount for each floor cleared, which stacks with the buffs the player selects.

==Cards==
===Normal Cards===
* +500 Stats: Gives 500 stat points in the stat that is shown.
* Cooldown Reduction: Reduces a certain skill or all skills of any weapon by 15% (Blox Fruit, Melee, etc.) or every move's cooldown by 10%.
* Skyjumps: The user gains two extra skyjumps.

===Special Cards===
* '''Shadow:''' Every 60 seconds, a shadow of the player with Godhuman spawns and attacks the enemies.
* '''35% HYPER!!:''' Melee, Sword, and Gun M1 cooldowns are reduced by 35%. Can be stacked.
* '''Overflow:''' Gives 3,000 extra overflow health, similar to Shark V4.
* '''Unbreakable:''' Attacks no longer break the user's ability charges.
* '''Fortress:''' Stuns no longer apply to the user, with a 20% chance to reflect 100% of damage dealt back to the attacker and stun them for 1 second.
* '''Lifesteal:''' Heals the user by 10% each time they hit an enemy. Can be stacked.
* '''30% Sniper:''' Gun damage and range become 30% stronger. Can be stacked.

