==Recommended Dungeon Build (PvE)==
While dungeons technically allow solo entry with the minimum player count, group synergy speeds up clears; coordinated teams generally outperform solo or under-filled groups, especially on higher difficulties.

===Fruit===
'''[[Buddha]]'''
* Relatively easy to obtain
* Provides strong survivability for long runs
* Has good reach for fighting multiple enemies at once

[[Buddha]] combined with [[Fox Lamp]] provides strong stun potential. [[Buddha]] combined with [[Cursed Dual Katana]] is commonly reported by players to be effective for clearing normal floors, as repeated M1 attacks while transformed can quickly defeat low-health, low-damage enemies.

'''Alternative / Team Synergy Options'''
* '''[[Dragon]]''' – A strong choice for dungeons, with effective M1 attacks and a large hitbox when transformed with '''[C] Scorching Downfall.''' For faster floor clears specifically, pairing Dragon with attack-speed buffs on M1 rather than pure damage buffs allows the fruit to clear regular floors more quickly, though this is less optimal for single-target boss damage.
* '''[[Dough]]''' – Provides strong crowd control and boss [[stun]] support. Fortress and Unbreakable help prevent the user from being stunned while using the '''[V] Dough Fist Fusillade/Restless Dough Barrage''' move.
* '''[[Kitsune]]''' – Has high DPS; pairing it with Cooldown Reduction and Ghoul V4's passive allows near-continuous skill use.
* '''[[Empyrean|Empyrean Kitsune]]''' – Similar to Kitsune, with access to '''[Z] Sweeping Firestorm''', one of the highest-damage moves in the game.
* '''[[Gravity]]''' – Provides strong enemy grouping with '''[C] Gravitational Prison.'''
* '''[[Sound]]''' – A support-focused fruit that buffs allies.
* '''[[Control]]''' – Deals fast, powerful damage. The '''[V] Total Concentration''' move stuns enemies for an extended duration without granting i-Frames, allowing other players to attack them while stunned. The drag M1 attack with the Spatial Cut Authentication admin panel upgrade equipped can also be very strong, as with the right placement of your domain, the attack will hit every enemy. (wherever you choose to cut, recommended to do so in line with the ground)
* '''[[Magma]]''' – Deals high damage over time with its abilities, useful for boss fights and for dealing with tougher enemies.
* '''[[Lightning]]''' – A good alternative to [[Dragon]]. The '''[V] Thunderball Destruction''' move has a large [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
* '''[[Spirit]]''' – Can spawn allies that regenerate health and increase the user's speed. Provides large AoE and high damage with '''[V] End of Times.'''
* '''[[Gas]]''' – Transformed M1 attacks can stun enemies continuously and pair well with the "15% more fruit M1 speed" buff, since Gas M1 attacks have no cooldown between each other. You become a monster.
* '''[[Phoenix]]''' – The Awakened and Transformed version of X can heal allies during boss fights and regular rooms. The V and F abilities allow the user to stay airborne and reach difficult areas such as shrines or vents, and the C move is useful against bosses.
* '''[[Tiger]]''' – Has moves that deal high damage and can grab multiple enemies. The C skill can be useful during boss fights, since the user can trigger the C cutscene while allies continue damaging the [[Bosses|boss]].
* '''[[Werewolf]]''' – Similar to [[Tiger]], but with higher damage.
* '''[[Pain]]''' – Most of its moves are multi-target, making it effective for dungeons.
* '''[[Mammoth]]''' – Provides AoE, good damage, and delayed stun with its C and X moves.
* '''[[Yeti]]''' – Has high DPS, and its transformed X move can destroy gas vents or Kitsune shrines effectively. Transformation is recommended.
* '''[[Shadow]]''' – Provides good DPS and damage over time with [V].
* '''[[Blizzard]]''' – All moves have decent AoE. '''[V] Blizzard Domain''' has a large AoE and high damage, and the [F] move can deal continuous damage when held.

