==Trivia==
* It was possible for [[Magic Elf|Elf NPCs]] to spawn in a dungeon during the Christmas event released alongside dungeons in [[Updates/29.0|Update 29]]. However, they sometimes would not drop [[Candy|Candies]], as NPCs do not drop anything in dungeons.
* [[Ice Castle]] [[NPCs]] in a dungeon can drop the [[Hidden Key|Hidden Key]], though the key is likely unusable, since there is no known openable gate in dungeons.
* The system message "The presents event will start in 10 minutes! Make sure you're in the green circle!" used to appear globally in dungeons (and the Simulation Hub) during the Christmas event when [[Updates/29.0|Update 29]] released. However, there was no event island in the dungeon's game instance, and the player could not obtain presents there.
* The total [[health]] of the Normal difficulty dungeon is just over seven million, and that of Hard is just over 20 million. This difference is mainly due to the difference in [[health]] of the bosses in these difficulties and the absence of the [[Bosses|boss]] [[Zero]] from Normal difficulty.
* A bug causes [[Dragon]] users' [[Power Meter|fury meter]] to drain to a negative value while destroying vents in transformed form.
* A bug allows dungeon bosses to instantly defeat a player they approach, using an invisible attack that deals an extreme amount of damage, enough to bypass any armor, defense, overflow health, or race abilities the player might have. This damage can be reflected back to the boss with a 20% chance if the player has '''Fortress''', or always with the [[Draco]] race's Thorn Mail gear (which reflects only part of the total damage). This instantly defeats the boss and gives the player a large increase in their total damage dealt.
* There is a very low chance that an enemy on a floor becomes invisible and cannot be found, making the dungeon impossible to complete. The invisible enemy sometimes still takes damage from attacks with large AoE and can be defeated by them, though this requires luck.
* [[Enchantments|Enchantements]] seem to don't work well inside dungeons. For example: Using the unreal unique enchantement that reduces cooldowns by 20%, doesn't seem to cumulate with [[Ghoul]] V4 (40% cooldowns redcution) and accesories that reduce cooldown for swords and guns. It has even been noticed that even with a total of 100% cooldown reduction on a move, it doesn't make you able to spam moves just like admins if you have the unreal enchantement (to be confirmed).
* There is currently a bug that allows a player thats under level 1100 to enter a dungeon by joining someone else's profile while they're already on the Dungeon Hub.

